(a) parametric corner exponent: integrand ~ r^(d/2 - nu - 1) near the soft corner; convergence iff nu < 2 - eps
   triangle            : nu = 1; corner integrand r^(-epsilon) dr; boundary of convergence eps = [1]; convergent at eps = 0: True
   bubble counterterm  : nu = 2; corner integrand r^(-epsilon - 1) dr; boundary of convergence eps = [0]; convergent at eps = 0: False
   bare bubble         : nu = epsilon + 2; corner integrand r^(-2*epsilon - 1) dr; boundary of convergence eps = [0]; convergent at eps = 0: False
   kite                : nu = 2*epsilon + 3; corner integrand r^(-3*epsilon - 2) dr; boundary of convergence eps = [-1/3]; convergent at eps = 0: False
   kite: Gamma(nu+2-d/2) = Gamma(3+3eps) finite; only the corner pole at eps = -1/3 -> DR value finite at eps = 0

(b) corner-cut integrals J(nu, delta) at eps = 0 (Q^2 = 1, m^2 = 0.01):
   nu=1 (triangle)                         : delta = 1e-4, 1e-6, 1e-8 -> ['24.760598', '24.770491', '24.77059']
   nu=2 (bubble counterterm)               : delta = 1e-4, 1e-6, 1e-8 -> ['56083.989', '102103.73', '148155.11']
   nu=2 with |ln F| (renormalized bubble)  : delta = 1e-4, 1e-6, 1e-8 -> ['598560.69', '1340338.9', '2294674.2']
   nu=3 (kite)                             : delta = 1e-4, 1e-6, 1e-8 -> ['9.7319902e+9', '9.9950652e+11', '9.9999281e+13']

