(d) soft power counting (connected hard complement): (M1) omega = n_a - V_S ; (M2) omega = 2 n_a
   single soft phi (triangle)                                                    : I_S=1, V_S=0, n_a=2:  omega(M1) = +2   omega(M2) = +4
   two soft rungs (planar/crossed two-loop ladder)                               : I_S=2, V_S=0, n_a=4:  omega(M1) = +4   omega(M2) = +8
   soft psi line + adjacent soft rung impossible (2 soft lines at a non-external vertex force the third)
   one-loop psi-bubble on a soft phi (bubble lines soft)                         : I_S=4, V_S=2, n_a=2:  omega(M1) = +0   omega(M2) = +4
   two-loop kite self-energy on a soft phi                                       : I_S=7, V_S=4, n_a=2:  omega(M1) = -2   omega(M2) = +4
   one-loop psi self-energy on a soft psi line (k -> p1)                         : I_S=4, V_S=2, n_a=2:  omega(M1) = +0   omega(M2) = +4
   soft psi triangle with three soft phi legs on the external psi lines (3 loops): I_S=6, V_S=3, n_a=3:  omega(M1) = +0   omega(M2) = +6
   soft psi box with four soft phi legs (4 loops)                                : I_S=8, V_S=4, n_a=4:  omega(M1) = +0   omega(M2) = +8
   (M1): omega <= 0 for every self-energy insertion on a line that can be soft and for soft vertex/box subgraphs;
   (M2) (phi^3_6, renormalizable): omega = 2 n_a > 0 for every soft subgraph with connected complement.
